# Build output
/holdfast
# The pre-rename binary name (TRANSCODE-12). Kept ignored deliberately: renaming this
# entry instead of adding to it un-ignored a stale ./transcode from an earlier build,
# and a blanket `git add` swept an 18MB binary into the commit. A blob in git history
# outlives a tag. Leave both.
/transcode
/dist/
/out/

# What a mutation run publishes (make mutation-diff / mutation-full). It is the record of
# ONE run on ONE machine - the score, the files mutated, the mutants that survived - and
# the run publishes it as a CI artifact. A copy committed here would be a measurement
# nobody re-derived, sitting beside a floor that is checked on every run.
/mutation-report.json*
/mutation-runner-report.json*

# Local state / runtime
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/state/

# Local config (never commit a real one — see config.example.yaml)
config.yaml
config.yml
*.local.yaml

# The credential files docs/docker.md and docker-compose.yml tell an operator to create
# beside the compose file. The control token is a hand-made string: it carries no vendor
# prefix, so no family in `make secret-scan` can recognise its CONTENT, and unlike `.env`
# its NAME is on no forbidden list either. Without this entry the one path this
# repository's own guidance names is the one path where a credential can be staged and
# the scanner still calls the tree clean.
control-token.txt
.env

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
